      <div class="help-acc-hdr-left">
        <div class="help-acc-icon" style="--c-tool:var(--c-help)"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13 2 4.5 13.5H11l-1 8.5 8.5-11.5H12z"/></svg></div>
        <div>
          <div class="help-acc-title">Quick Start — pick your path</div>
          <div class="help-acc-sub">Four paths · under 2 minutes each</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <svg class="help-acc-chevron" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="5 8 10 13 15 8"/></svg>
    </button>
    <div class="help-acc-body">
      <div class="help-acc-inner">
        <p class="help-p">Every path below produces a ready-to-run VuGen script ZIP in under 2 minutes. Choose the one that matches your starting point.</p>
        <div class="help-paths">
          <div class="help-path" style="--c-tool:var(--c-convert)">
            <div class="help-path-title"><svg class="help-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 3H7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2 2 2 0 0 1 2 2v4a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h1M16 3h1a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v4a2 2 0 0 0 2 2 2 2 0 0 0-2 2v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2h-1"/></svg>Path A — Postman / Bruno</div>
            <ol class="help-path-steps">
              <li>Click <strong>Postman / Bruno</strong> in the sidebar</li>
              <li>Upload your .json / .yml / .bru file</li>
              <li>Choose output format → <strong>Convert</strong></li>
              <li>Download ZIP → open in VuGen</li>
            </ol>
          </div>
          <div class="help-path" style="--c-tool:var(--c-jmeter)">
            <div class="help-path-title"><svg class="help-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M17 3l4 4-4 4"/><path d="M3 7h18"/><path d="M7 21l-4-4 4-4"/><path d="M21 17H3"/></svg>Path B — JMeter (.jmx)</div>
            <ol class="help-path-steps">
              <li>Click <strong>JMeter</strong> in the sidebar</li>
              <li>Upload your .jmx file + any CSV files</li>
              <li>Choose output format → <strong>Convert</strong></li>
              <li>Download ZIP → open in VuGen</li>
            </ol>
          </div>
          <div class="help-path" style="--c-tool:var(--c-record)">
            <div class="help-path-title"><svg class="help-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3.5" fill="currentColor"/></svg>Path C — Record in browser</div>
            <ol class="help-path-steps">
              <li>Click <strong>Recorder</strong> in the sidebar</li>
              <li>Get the CDP Recorder — or install the bookmarklet (one-time)</li>
              <li>Record your journey (CDP Recorder toolbar, or F12 → Network)</li>
              <li>Export HAR → upload to Recorder</li>
              <li>Generate Script → Download ZIP</li>
            </ol>
          </div>
          <div class="help-path" style="--c-tool:var(--c-studio)">
            <div class="help-path-title"><svg class="help-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"/><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"/></svg>Path D — Deep correlation</div>
            <ol class="help-path-steps">
              <li>Click <strong>Script Studio</strong> in the sidebar</li>
              <li>Record the same journey twice → two HARs</li>
              <li>Upload both → <strong>Analyze</strong></li>
              <li>Review Advisor → Accept → Regenerate</li>
              <li>Download ZIP → open in VuGen</li>
            </ol>
